# Who gets asked to look at what. GitHub requests review from the owners of
# every path a pull request touches, which is how a change to the release
# gate or the security policy stops being something that can land unseen.
#
# One maintainer today, so every line resolves to the same person. The file is
# still worth keeping explicit: it is the list to edit when that changes, and
# it makes the ownership of the load-bearing paths visible rather than assumed.

# Everything, unless a later rule is more specific.
*                           @saworbit

# The release gate and everything that runs with a repository token.
/.github/                   @saworbit
/.github/workflows/         @saworbit

# The build and packaging contract. The version in CMakeLists.txt is the
# source every document is validated against.
/CMakeLists.txt             @saworbit
/cmake/                     @saworbit

# The protocol surface. Changing a tool name, schema or annotation changes
# what every connected agent is allowed to do without asking.
/src/mcp/                   @saworbit
/include/didi/mcp/          @saworbit
/schemas/                   @saworbit

# Security posture and the promises made about it.
/SECURITY.md                @saworbit
/THIRD_PARTY.md             @saworbit
/LICENSE                    @saworbit
